{"assets":["/statement-assets/b30bdbd004eaf1cd540e48f76daaab093f989cc7e4b39925c4141771c02cbf23.png","/statement-assets/e05c873d8b69472429ae4be52bb9eb38e2518196a54d81746370a0772491b6fb.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"959","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Mahmoud and Ehab and the wrong algorithm"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Mahmoud was trying to solve the vertex cover problem on trees. The problem statement is:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given an undirected tree consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" nodes, find the minimum number of vertices that cover all the edges. Formally, we need to find a set of vertices such that for each edge "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(u, v)"},{"kind":"text","text":" that belongs to the tree, either "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" is in the set, or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" is in the set, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"or both are in the set"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Mahmoud has found the following algorithm:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Root the tree at node "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Count the number of nodes at an even depth. Let it be "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"evenCnt"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Count the number of nodes at an odd depth. Let it be "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"oddCnt"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The answer is the minimum between "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"evenCnt"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"oddCnt"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The depth of a node in a tree is the number of edges in the shortest path between this node and the root. The depth of the root is 0."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ehab told Mahmoud that this algorithm is wrong, but he didn't believe because he had tested his algorithm against many trees and it worked, so Ehab asked you to find 2 trees consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" nodes. The algorithm should find an incorrect answer for the first tree and a correct answer for the second one."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line contains an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2 ≤ n ≤ 105)"},{"kind":"text","text":", the number of nodes in the desired trees."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The output should consist of 2 "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"independent"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" sections, each containing a tree. The algorithm should find an incorrect answer for the tree in the first section and a correct answer for the tree in the second. If a tree doesn't exist for some section, output \"-1\" (without quotes) "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"for that section only"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If the answer for a section exists, it should contain "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines, each containing 2 space-separated integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ u, v ≤ n)"},{"kind":"text","text":", which means that there's an undirected edge between node "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" and node "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":". If the given graph isn't a tree or it doesn't follow the format, you'll receive wrong answer verdict."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple answers, you can print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1\n1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"8\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 2\n1 3\n2 4\n2 5\n3 6\n4 7\n4 8\n1 2\n1 3\n2 4\n2 5\n2 6\n3 7\n6 8"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, there is only 1 tree with 2 nodes (node "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" connected to node "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The algorithm will produce a correct answer in it so we printed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":" - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the first section, but notice that we printed this tree in the second section."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first tree, the algorithm will find an answer with 4 nodes, while there exists an answer with 3 nodes like this: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b30bdbd004eaf1cd540e48f76daaab093f989cc7e4b39925c4141771c02cbf23.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" In the second tree, the algorithm will find an answer with 3 nodes which is correct: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/e05c873d8b69472429ae4be52bb9eb38e2518196a54d81746370a0772491b6fb.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"959C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/959/problem/C"}